msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:27
msgid ""
"Work in a virtual environment. The engine is a compiled extension, and "
"mixing it with a system Python is the fastest way to an import error "
"nobody can reproduce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The repository's `Makefile` does the whole thing, virtual environment "
"included:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:39
msgid ""
"A format author wants the tooling as well, which is one target rather "
"than three commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:45
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`make help` lists the rest, and {doc}`../guides/engine/build` explains "
"the arrangement. If anything looks off, `make doctor` says what is "
"installed, what is missing, and which target supplies it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:48
msgid "The same thing by hand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:49
msgid ""
"Nothing above is magic, and none of it is required — the targets are "
"recipes of ordinary commands, which is what you want if you are "
"installing into an environment the Makefile knows nothing about:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:60
msgid ""
"The engine is built by [maturin](https://www.maturin.rs/) because of the "
"Rust extension; the two tooling packages are plain setuptools projects. "
"For an editable install while working on the crate itself, use maturin "
"directly — `maturin develop` rebuilds the extension in place, and "
"`--release` is worth the extra compile time for anything but the smallest"
" report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:70
msgid ""
"`freeports-validate` does **not** require the engine: verifying somebody "
"else's grants should not mean installing a PDF extractor. The one thing "
"it gives up without it is reading its settings from the freeports "
"configuration file, which needs the engine's knowledge of where such a "
"file lives. To have that tier as well:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:79
msgid "A format author installing all three has it anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:81
msgid "The `freeports` binary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:83
msgid ""
"`pip install` and `maturin develop` build the *extension module*, not the"
" command-line binary: the two are separate build products of one crate, "
"and neither implies the other. This is the usual reason an installation "
"ends up half-done — the module imports and the command is nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:87
msgid "`make install` covers both. Done by hand it is a cargo build and a copy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:95
msgid ""
"By default `make install-binary` puts it in the active environment's "
"`bin/`, so that uninstalling is complete; `make install-binary "
"PREFIX=/usr/local` installs it system-wide instead, and `DESTDIR` is "
"honoured for packaging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:99
msgid ""
"Everything the binary does is also reachable from Python through the same"
" crate, so this step is optional if you drive the engine as a library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:102
msgid "Checking the installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:108
msgid "which is these two questions, and says nothing if both work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:115
msgid ""
"Both should answer. If the second fails while the first works, the binary"
" is on your `PATH` but the extension is not in *this* interpreter's "
"environment — almost always a virtual environment that is not the one the"
" install went into."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/install.md:119
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A working installation is not yet a working run: two inputs must exist "
"first, and neither ships with the engine. See "
"{doc}`../guides/user/inputs`."
